---
code: munge-name-collision
when-fires: two DISTINCT source names munge to one sh funcname. oracle/reserved.rs. `{count}` interpolates twice (the count and the funcdef count).
why: non-injective munge: refuse-and-run (never silently last-writer-wins).
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- munge-name-collision && mise run loom:promote -- munge-name-collision`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all munge-name-collision` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
# Two spellings of one tool's name. Dots and hyphens both munge to `_`, so the two funcdefs
# would emit the same sh function.
hork.tool__predict() {
   hork --query "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 : sm.dorc.Package:"$1"@installed
}

hork-tool__predict() {
   hork --query "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 : sm.dorc.Package:"$1"@installed
}

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
